Chapter: SignStdio
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Ed25519
  cites Foreword chapter Sha512

Section: Helpers

  take-range : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  take-range (bs) (i) (stop) (acc) =
   if i >= stop then acc
   else take-range bs (i + 1) stop (list-push acc (list-at bs i))

  splice-at : List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  splice-at (bs) (at) (patch) =
   (take-range bs 0 at []) & patch & (take-range bs (at + list-length patch) (list-length bs) [])

Section: Body

 The payload is a mode byte then a 32-byte Ed25519 seed. Mode 0 answers the
 seed's 32-byte public key. Mode 1 carries a CDX after the seed and answers
 the same CDX signed: the header's content hash sits at bytes 8..39 and
 deliberately excludes the signature, the author key is written at 40..71
 and the signature over the hash at 72..135, which is the layout build.ps1's
 sign phase writes and CdxVerifier.codex reads.

  plug-emit-bytes : Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  plug-emit-bytes (payload-buf) (payload-len) =
   if payload-len < 33 then print-line-uni ("REFUSED short payload " & show payload-len)
   else let mode = peek-byte payload-buf 0
   in if mode > 1 then print-line-uni ("REFUSED unknown mode " & show mode)
   else let payload = __buf-read-bytes payload-buf 0 payload-len
   in let key = take-range payload 1 33 []
   in let pub = ed25519-public-key key
   in if mode == 0 then write-binary pub
   else if payload-len < 169 then print-line-uni ("REFUSED mode 1 payload " & show payload-len & " is shorter than a CDX header")
   else let cdx = take-range payload 33 payload-len []
   in let hash = take-range cdx 8 40 []
   in let sig = ed25519-sign key pub hash
   in write-binary (splice-at (splice-at cdx 40 pub) 72 sig)
